# Defense in depth: uploads/avatars/ and uploads/offers/ are meant to be
# publicly *readable* (images/docs), but nothing here should ever be
# *executable* — even though the upload endpoints already whitelist
# extensions strictly, this ensures a bug there can't turn into RCE.
# uploads/verification/ already has its own "Require all denied" (no direct
# access at all); this is redundant-but-harmless there.
Options -Indexes

<FilesMatch "\.(php|php3|php4|php5|php7|phtml|pl|py|cgi|sh|asp|aspx|exe)$">
  Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
